  "description": "POV: you pay your monthly Spotify bill. Follow the money to the music industry.\n\nSources:\n- Spotify Newsroom: 2025 music industry payouts (Loud & Clear, Jan 28, 2026): https://newsroom.spotify.com/2026-01-28/2025-music-industry-payouts-whats-next-for-artists/\n- Spotify: Premium plans (Individual plan price): https://www.spotify.com/us/premium/\n\nFrom the cited pages: Spotify paid more than $11 billion to the music industry in 2025 and says it pays out two-thirds of all music revenue to the industry, almost 70% of what it takes in; the Individual Premium plan costs $12.99 a month in the United States. Our math: $12.99 x 70% = about $9.09, so about $9 goes to the music industry and about $4 stays with Spotify; $11 billion / 365 = about $30.1 million a day; $11 billion / 31.5 million seconds = about $349 a second (both are minimums because the payout was more than $11 billion). Not financial advice.\n\n#shorts #spotify #music #howtheymakemoney",
